# Review routing.
#
# Everything currently routes to the single maintainer of the organisation. The file exists
# anyway, for two reasons that are worth writing down:
#
#   1. Branch protection requires an approving review. Without CODEOWNERS GitHub still
#      allows that review, but there is no recorded answer to "who owns this path", and the
#      answer only gets harder to reconstruct as the repository grows.
#   2. When a second maintainer joins, the split is an edit to this file rather than a
#      research task. The obvious splits, when they are needed, are: `/contracts/` and
#      `/scripts/` (on-chain and deployment), `/backend/`, `/frontend/`, and
#      `/.github/workflows/` together with `SECURITY.md`.
#
# Paths use the last matching pattern, so a more specific rule added later overrides this one.

